	exttt{SEAM.E8.DISCRIMINATOR.01}: the empirical/structural DISCRIMINATOR bundle (mode D of the \vref{v347} closure-mode classification) --- concrete FALSIFIABLE kill tests separating the claimed seam $=(E_8)_1$ from the nearest $c{=}8$ rival $SO(16)_1{=}(D_8)_1$. \mE\mX\ PRIMARY/GSD: $|\!\det\mathrm{Cartan}(E_8)|{=}1$ (ONE primary, holomorphic) vs $|\!\det\mathrm{Cartan}(D_8)|{=}4$ (FOUR primaries $1,v,s,c$); torus GSD $=\#$primaries $=1$ vs $4$ --- a seam with GSD$>1$ falsifies $(E_8)_1$. \mE\mX\ CURRENT/THETA: level-1 current count $\dim E_8{=}248$ vs $\dim SO(16){=}120$; the $E_8$ lattice theta has $240$ norm-2 roots ($={}112$ integer $+128$ spinor, computed) vs $D_8$'s $112$ --- current spectrum and lattice theta DIFFER. \mE\ $c{=}8$ IS NOT A DISCRIMINATOR: both have $c{=}8$ (the \vref{v277} ambiguity); only the order-4 mu4 condensation + $\det K{=}1$ (the genus-1 statement, \vref{v90}) selects $E_8$. \mE\ NON-VACUITY: the discriminators all fire on the rival ($\det4{
e}1$, currents $120{
e}248$, roots $112{
e}240$). \mX\mC\ mode D realised as concrete kill tests; 	exttt{SEAM.EQUIV.01} stays \mO\ (the discriminators distinguish the TARGET but do not PROVE the seam realises it). Python-only (numpy; the dets Wolfram-mirrored via \vref{v89}/\vref{v281}/\vref{v422}). \mE\mC\mO\mX

	exttt{SEAM.S3.LTO.01}: the EXPLICIT flat-band commuting-projector (local-topological-order) realisation of the S3 input --- advancing \vref{v424} sub-step (i) (``realise the raw seam as a $\Z_2$-reflection commuting-projector LTO'') from abstract existence to an explicit gap-protected quasi-local projector net carrying the $\Z_2$ reflection and the $\mu_4$ clock. \mE\ FLAT-BAND PARENT: the flattened Bloch $Q{=}h/|h|$ of \vref{v367}'s $p{+}ip$ collar has $Q^2{=}I$ (flat $\pm1$ bands) and $P{=}(I{-}Q)/2$ is an exact projector EQUAL to the occupied ground-state projector --- a frustration-free commuting-projector parent with the same gapped ground state. \mE\ GAP-PROTECTED QUASI-LOCALITY: the gapped projector kernel $|P(n,0)|$ decays rapidly ($\xi{\approx}1.14$ at $M{=}1$, exp $R^2{=}0.995$, $|P(20,0)|{<}10^{-6}$) and $\xi$ GROWS as the gap closes ($2.7$ at gap $0.02$); at the GAPLESS point the kernel decays as a clean power law $|R|^{-2.1}$ ($R^2{=}0.999$, tail ${\sim}2{	imes}10^{-4}$) --- locality needs the gap. \mE\ $\Z_2$ REFLECTION $+$ $\mu_4$ INHERITED: the flattened modular Hamiltonian $K_{\mathrm{flat}}{=}\operatorname{sign}(K)$ inherits $\Theta K_{\mathrm{flat}}\Theta{=}{-}K_{\mathrm{flat}}$ (BW, $u_\Theta{=}J$) and $[ho,K_{\mathrm{flat}}]{=}0$ ($\mu_4$) EXACTLY ($\operatorname{sign}$ is odd; $ho$ commutes with any $f(K)$). \mE\ NEG CONTROLS: a side-even reflection gives $2\|K_{\mathrm{flat}}\|{
eq}0$ (BW fails), an off-$\mu_4$ $K$ mixing opposite-sign marks breaks $[ho,\operatorname{sign}(K)]{
eq}0$. \mC\mO\ the chiral $c_-{=}8{
eq}0$ (FHS Chern $|C|{=}1$) obstructs STRICT finite-range commuting-projector locality (Kapustin--Fidkowski, 	exttt{arXiv:1810.07756}; $C{
eq}0$ forbids exponentially-localised Wannier, Thouless), so the realisation is the quasi-local LTO net of NPW26 --- the form sub-step (i) asks for. 	exttt{SEAM.EQUIV.01} stays \mO\ (the continuum theorem MMST \vref{v336} is the backbone). Python-only (numpy; the det/level discriminators Wolfram-mirrored via \vref{v89}/\vref{v281}/\vref{v422}). \mE\mC\mO

	exttt{SEAM.S3.LOCALITY.01}: the Kapustin--Fidkowski/Thouless strict-locality OBSTRUCTION made explicit --- sharpening \vref{v460}'s verdict from a cited statement to an EXHIBITED topological obstruction on the same \vref{v367} $p{+}ip$ collar. \mE\ CHERN INTEGER: the FHS Chern is $C{=}{+}1$ (chiral $M{=}1$), $0$ (trivial $M{=}3$), $-1$ (opposite mass) --- the invertible-phase invariant. \mE\ WILSON-LOOP / WANNIER-CENTRE WINDING $={}$ CHERN: the hybrid Wannier centre $	heta(k_y)$ winds by $|C|{=}1$ (chiral) and $0$ (trivial) over the BZ; exponentially-localised Wannier functions exist IFF the winding is $0$ (Brouder--Panati et al., PRL 98 046402; Thouless), so the chiral collar has NONE. \mE\ OBSTRUCTION INTEGERS TIED: winding $={}|C|{=}1{
eq}0$ and $c_-{=}16/2{=}8{=}\gcar{+}\Nfam{=}\operatorname{rank}E_8{
eq}0$ (the same $8$ as $c_3$'s one-sided count, \vref{v456}). \mE\ NEG CONTROL: BOTH phases are gapped, yet only the trivial (winding $0$) admits exp-localised Wannier and a strict finite-range commuting projector --- it is the CHIRALITY, not the gap. \mC\mO\ Kapustin--Fidkowski (	exttt{arXiv:1810.07756}): a strictly finite-range commuting projector would force winding $0$, $C{=}0$; since $C{=}1{
eq}0$ NONE exists, so \vref{v424} sub-step (i)'s realisation is PROVABLY the quasi-local NPW26 LTO net (strict locality topologically forbidden, not a missing premise) --- upgrading \vref{v460}'s cited verdict. 	exttt{SEAM.EQUIV.01} stays \mO\ (continuum theorem MMST \vref{v336} the backbone). Python-only (numpy; the winding/Chern integers Lean-mirrored, 	exttt{SeamResidualAxiom.lean}). \mE\mC\mO

	exttt{CELEST.WP2.01}: WP2 of the celestial-holographic research contract 	exttt{CELEST.SEAM.01} --- the clock-invariant deformation $XY{=}Z^4{+}a_0$ of the $A_3$ seam orbifold: geometry, periods/monodromy, deformed algebra (Bittleston--Homans--Sharma $\Z_2	o\Z_4$ transfer, 	exttt{arXiv:2305.09451}). Sympy exact. \mE\ GEOMETRY: $P(iZ){=}P(Z)$ forces $a_3{=}a_2{=}a_1{=}0$ SHARPLY (two-sided: $\prod_k(Z-i^kw){=}Z^4{-}w^4$); smooth iff $a_0{
eq}0$ ($\operatorname{disc}{=}256\,a_0^3$); branch points $Z^4{=}{-}a_0$ $=$ ONE free $\mu_4$ orbit in every fibre; cross-ratio $2$ / $j{=}1728$ for ALL $a_0$ (binary-quartic invariants $I{=}12a_0$, $J{=}0$ identically) $\Rightarrow$ $a_0$ is a PURE SCALE, the $	au{=}i$ pillowcase (\vref{v168}/\vref{v214}) is FROZEN --- no shape modulus. \mE\ PERIODS: $\Pi{=}t(i{-}1)(1,i,i^2)$, all $3$ vanishing spheres carry the SAME volume $\sqrt2\,t$ (lockstep); the clock on $H_2$ is a COXETER element of $W(A_3)$ (char $x^3{+}x^2{+}x{+}1$, eigenvalues $\{i,-1,-i\}$ $=$ the $A_3$ exponents $1,2,3$; $h(A_3){=}4{=}|\mu_4|{=}\Nfam{+}1$); NO invariant cycle ($\det(A{-}1){=}{-}4$); the surviving direction is the weight-$1$ $\chi_1$-Fourier diagonal $(1,i,i^2)$, NOT the naive invariant diagonal; the clock IS the Picard--Lefschetz monodromy of the family ($a_0	o e^{2\pi i}a_0$ gives the $4$-cycle); versal weights $(a_3,a_2,a_1,a_0){=}(1,2,3,0)$ $=$ the REGULAR $\mu_4$ representation, invariant line $=a_0$ alone. \mE\ ALGEBRA ($\Z_2	o\Z_4$): mode dictionary $\{w[m,n]:m{\equiv}n mod4\}\leftrightarrow\{X^pY^qZ^r:r{\le}3\}$; bracket $\{f,g\}{=}{-}4\,\mathrm{Nambu}(XY{-}Z^4{-}a_0)$ anchored at the $a_0{=}0$ orbifold w-sector ($\{X,Y\}{=}16Z^3$, $\{Y,Z\}{=}{-}4Y$, $\{Z,X\}{=}{-}4X$), Jacobi $+$ Casimir exact, uniform clock-degree $-1$; S-algebra corrections exactly LINEAR in $a_0$ at the $\Z_4$ wrap $r{+}r'{\ge}4$, grade-conserving (NO sector leak $\Rightarrow$ the \vref{v492} equivariant SDYM($E_8$) sector deforms consistently); $a_0\leftrightarrow$ the BHS $c^2$ slot (weight $0$); matrix factorisations (McKay modules) deform along every $1{+}3$ and $2{+}2$ orbit splitting; the clock fixes exactly the antipodal $2{+}2$ sector (the EH/$\Z_2$ middle node, $4{=}2{	imes}2$). \mE\ NEGATIVE CONTROLS: $a_1Z\Rightarrow j{=}0$ (hexagonal CM point); pure $a_2Z^2$ stays SINGULAR ($A_1$ node); $a_2{
eq}0\Rightarrow j{=}1556068/81{
eq}1728$ (exact instance, two routes agree); grading leak explicit ($Z^2{\cdot}Z^2$ picks up grades $\{0,1,2\}$). \mC\ three NAMED identifications (verdict B, not A): $-4\,$Nambu $=$ THE $k{=}4$ CCA bracket (BHS prove $k{=}2$); period $=$ root difference (A-series residue normalisation); the seam-scale reading of $a_0$ presupposes the WP1 bridge clock$^2{=}$deck ($\Z_8$, $8{=}2|\mu_4|$). \mC\ \vref{v216} PRECISION (typed, NO marker move): given the order-$4$ clock, the clock-invariant deformation freezes the $(2,2,2,2)$ modulus to the square AUTOMATICALLY --- a relocation of the same order-$4$ input (the clock IS the carrier input), not a new derivation; v216 stays \mO. \mO\ full deformed twisted-sector OPEs, the $W(\mu)$-type scaling limit for $k{=}4$, the spacetime splitting-function check, WP3--WP5; 	exttt{SEAM.EQUIV.01} stays \mO, untouched. Exact (sympy). \mE\mC\mO
